From the latest 'Scraps' on
META's Muse and the agent race:

@StockSavvyShay and @StockMarketNerd reported $AMZN blocked Muse from shopping on its site citing terms violations - with Meta insisting Muse never sees passwords or payment details and @StockMarketNerd expecting a settlement - while @realroseceline argued the block is about protecting high-margin advertising dollars since you can't show an ad to a robot.

@StockSavvyShay reported $SHOP will bring Shop Pay agentic checkout into Muse across every Shopify store, letting users buy directly inside the assistant.

@ChrisCamillo went levered long $META on Friday and Monday for roughly $1M - his second most profitable single-day trade in 20 years - and calls $AMZN the off-radar Muse beneficiary given Meta's use of AWS Bedrock and commitments to tens of millions of Graviton CPU cores.

@babyfolio expects $META to double once Muse reaches earnings, while @Brian_Stoffel_ and @StockMarketNerd point to a cheap valuation, the AI advertising payoff and the optionality to resell unused compute if the bets fail.

@zephyr_z9 said Meta kept Muse out of WhatsApp because it lacks the CPUs, GPUs, DRAM and SSDs needed to serve 2 billion users.

@WealthyReadings argued OpenAI and Anthropic sell intelligence but lack distribution, while $GOOGL and $META can turn models into enterprise products and cash.

